---
import ProviderPlaybookTemplate from '../components/ProviderPlaybookTemplate.astro';
const data = {
 "kind": "troubleshooting",
 "name": "Plesk (hosting)",
 "title": "Plesk (hosting) DNS Problems: Common Issues and Fixes",
 "description": "The most common Plesk (hosting) DNS problems, from broken mail to SERVFAIL, with the diagnosis and fix for each.",
 "intro": "Most Plesk (hosting) DNS complaints collapse into the same handful of causes. Match your symptom below; every fix includes the free tool that confirms it.",
 "issues": [
  [
   "Records exist but don't answer",
   "Plesk DNS is disabled for that domain, or nameservers point elsewhere. One source of truth only."
  ],
  [
   "Mail breaks after enabling external DNS",
   "Mail records live in Plesk's zone; recreate MX/SPF/DKIM at the external DNS host when you move."
  ],
  [
   "DNS template changes did nothing",
   "Templates only affect newly created domains; edit the existing zone's records."
  ]
 ],
 "quirk": "Plesk can disable its DNS per domain (Tools, DNS Settings, Disable). When disabled, the panel still shows the template records, which do nothing: the classic Plesk trap.",
 "faqs": [
  [
   "Should Plesk or Cloudflare hold DNS?",
   "External anycast DNS (Cloudflare etc.) is more resilient than a single hosting server; keep Plesk DNS only for simplicity's sake."
  ],
  [
   "How long do DNS changes take in Plesk (hosting)?",
   "The provider serves new values quickly, but resolvers keep old answers until each record's TTL expires. Verify live values with the record lookup, then watch the propagation checker until resolvers agree."
  ],
  [
   "Where do I find Plesk (hosting)'s nameservers?",
   "This playbook's nameservers guide covers the exact location. They are the delegation pair your registrar must point at for {name} to be authoritative."
  ],
  [
   "Should I lower TTL before changing records in Plesk (hosting)?",
   "Yes, for anything planned: set TTL to 300 seconds at least one old-TTL cycle ahead, make the change, confirm propagation, then restore the TTL."
  ],
  [
   "Can I keep email with one provider and DNS in Plesk (hosting)?",
   "Yes: DNS host and mail provider are independent. Publish the mail provider's MX, SPF, DKIM, and DMARC records in {name}, and keep those records unproxied."
  ],
  [
   "Which records should every domain have?",
   "A (and ideally AAAA) for the website, MX plus SPF/DKIM/DMARC for mail, and CAA to restrict certificate issuance. Everything else is per-service."
  ]
 ],
 "related": [
  [
   "DNS record types reference",
   "/dns-records/"
  ],
  [
   "TTL explained",
   "/what-is-ttl-in-dns/"
  ]
 ]
};
---
<ProviderPlaybookTemplate data={data} />
